![medium](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/medium-priority.svg)

When indexing blockers into a map by `question_group_key`, we should normalize the input collection using `asArray`, filter out non-record entries, and ensure only entries with a non-empty key string are indexed to prevent malformed or empty keys.

```javascript
  for (const blocker of asArray(blockers).filter((b) => isRecord(b) && isNonEmptyString(b.question_group_key))) {
    const list = byGroup.get(blocker.question_group_key) ?? [];
    list.push(blocker);
    byGroup.set(blocker.question_group_key, list);
  }
```

<details>
<summary>References</summary>

1. When indexing assets or records into a map/object by an ID, normalize the input collection using an array helper (e.g., `asArray`), filter out non-record entries, and ensure only entries with a non-empty ID string are indexed to prevent malformed or empty keys.
</details>

