![medium](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/medium-priority.svg)

Ensure the validator fails closed gracefully on missing or malformed source artifact manifests and upstream parse diagnostics. We should explicitly verify that `inputs.diagnostics` has no errors, and that `inputs.questionLevelLocator` and `inputs.pageScreenshotAssets` are present and carry valid array fields.

```javascript
  if (Array.isArray(inputs.diagnostics) && inputs.diagnostics.length > 0) {
    for (const diag of inputs.diagnostics) {
      pushError(errors, diag.code || 'upstream_diagnostic_error', diag.path || '/', diag.reason || 'Upstream parse diagnostic');
    }
  }

  if (!isRecord(inputs.questionLevelLocator)) {
    pushError(errors, 'upstream_locator_missing', '/', 'Upstream question-level locator is missing or malformed');
  } else if (inputs.questionLevelLocator.rows !== undefined && !Array.isArray(inputs.questionLevelLocator.rows)) {
    pushError(errors, 'upstream_locator_rows_invalid_type', '/rows', 'Upstream locator rows must be an array');
  }

  if (!isRecord(inputs.pageScreenshotAssets)) {
    pushError(errors, 'upstream_page_screenshot_assets_missing', '/', 'Upstream page screenshot assets are missing or malformed');
  } else if (inputs.pageScreenshotAssets.page_assets !== undefined && !Array.isArray(inputs.pageScreenshotAssets.page_assets)) {
    pushError(errors, 'upstream_page_assets_invalid_type', '/page_assets', 'Upstream page assets must be an array');
  }

```

<details>
<summary>References</summary>

1. Ensure validators fail closed gracefully on missing or malformed source artifact manifests and upstream parse diagnostics.
2. When validating expected array fields in input data, if a field is present but is not an array, record a validation failure (blocker) and process it as an empty array. This prevents TypeErrors during execution while ensuring the system fails closed.
</details>

